//? Title: Bucket Sort: Distribution, Order and Actual Work
//? Subtitle: Checked integer scattering, the original occupancy experiment, and a matched-occupancy counterexample
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Bucket sort uses values to scatter items into ordered ranges, sorts each range,
and gathers the results. We retain the original seven-integer example and the
100-item uniform-versus-clustered experiment. Native C++ now supplies the exact
scatter mapping, actual bucket snapshots, insertion comparisons and shifts,
and reproducible-toolchain synthetic inputs. A second experiment holds every
bucket occupancy fixed while changing input order: one case is linear and the
other quadratic. Occupancy bounds the work, but does not determine it. All
programs also support the complete signed 32-bit integer range without overflow.
)

\toc

> A small scatter, insertion sort and gather

The input [5,3,8,1,9,2,7] has minimum 1, maximum 9 and inclusive span 9.
For n items, this implementation uses n buckets and maps a value x to

\[
b(x)=\left\lfloor\frac{(x-\min)n}{\max-\min+1}\right\rfloor.
\]

For example b(5)=3 and b(9)=6. Bucket two is empty; values 1 and 2 share
bucket zero. That bucket is already ordered, so its insertion sort performs
one false predecessor-greater-than-key comparison and no shifts. The diagram
and table use records from the actual sorting kernel, rather than recomputing
occupancy in the report.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/bucket_sort_pipeline.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto trace=dm::algorithms::bucket_sort_trace({5,3,8,1,9,2,7});
  if (trace.output!=std::vector<int>{1,2,3,5,7,8,9}) return 1;
  std::string contents="actual scatter buckets";
  std::print("| bucket | encounter order | sorted contents | key comparisons | shifts | final key stores |\n"
             "| ---: | :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for (std::size_t b=0;b<trace.buckets.size();++b) {
    const auto& row=trace.buckets[b];
    contents+=std::format("\nb{}: {}",b,row.input);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",b,row.input,row.output,row.key_comparisons,row.shifts,row.placements);
  }
  dm::graphics::Diagram diagram(65,1100);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle style;style.width=3.8;style.height=2.0;
  diagram.node("input",{0,0},"input\n[5,3,8,1,9,2,7]",style);
  style.width=3.6;style.height=4.6;
  diagram.node("buckets",{5.5,0},contents,style);
  style.width=3.8;style.height=2.0;style.fill={220,252,231};
  diagram.node("output",{11,0},std::format("ascending output\n{}",trace.output),style)
      .edge("input","buckets","scatter")
      .edge("buckets","output","sort, gather")
      .text({5.5,-3.2},std::format("inclusive range [{},{}]; {} buckets",trace.minimum,trace.maximum,trace.bucket_count))
      .save_svg("build/bucket_sort_pipeline.svg");
  std::print("\nInput destinations: {}. Sorted: {}.\n",trace.bucket_of_input,trace.output);
  std::print("Occupied buckets: {}; maximum load: {}; sum of squared loads: {}.\n",
      trace.nonempty_buckets,trace.max_occupancy,trace.occupancy_square_sum);
}
```
